    FEAT-0001: the bookings file says which format version it uses
    
    Facilities' other tools read data/bookings.json too, and they want to
    be able to change its format later. The file is now an object with a
    version and the list of bookings: { "version": 2, "bookings": [...] }.
    
    No rule changed: the 2-hour limit, overlaps, and the per-day cap work
    exactly as before. Every test changed anyway. Each one hands
    FakeFileSystem a JSON string, or reads back the JSON that book() wrote,
    so each one knew the file's format, and each one had to learn the new
    one.

